# RoboCarl (AI brief)

Prefer this over codebase exploration. Open specific files only when editing them. **Update this rule** when levels, systems, or folder layout change.

## Game
2D URP portrait puzzle, playfield **9×19.5** (`AspectRatioCamera`). Player does **not** control Carl — Carl walks to closest **LOS-visible** oil/battery; player uses **draggable** or **button** walls, plus **power buttons** for devices. Energy drains ~100s idle / ~25s walking (same pool); oil drains with walk. Energy 0 → lose. WinLine → MainMenu.

## Levels
Shared base scene only: `SampleScene` (split floors, L1 ground Spring, WinLine, Carl). Each level applies its own `LevelNLayout` + `Resources/LevelNSpawns` — keep those assets separate; do not assume elevated L1 props are “L2 leftovers.”

| Level | Path | Notes |
|------:|------|-------|
| 1 | `LevelSession=1` → `SampleScene` | `Level1Layout` + `Level1Spawns`: ground oil + ground battery; one-way + platform spring + platform battery. Scene keeps floors + ground Spring + WinLine + Carl |
| 2 | `LevelSession=2` → **same** `SampleScene` | `Level2Layout` (full floor, strip scene Spring) + `Level2Spawns`: left battery+spring, right ground battery+spikes, one-way, platform oil/spring/battery, `DraggableWall`, `ButtonWall` |
| 3 | `LevelSession=3` → **same** `SampleScene` | `Level3Layout` + `Level3Spawns` (+ fans/buttons in layout code). Buttonless dual doors + `LinkedWallButton`; side springs/one-ways; left ceiling spikes; upward fan under right one-way; side fans |
| 4 | `LevelSession=4` → **same** `SampleScene` | `Level4Layout` (full floor, strip scene Spring + WinLine, Carl feet on start platform) + `Level4Spawns`: horizontal `DraggableWall`; right-facing spring on left; up-springs under platform; one-way above platform (WIP, no pickups/WinLine yet) |

- Menu levels 1–4 only (`MainMenuController`). Play Mode starts on `MainMenu`.
- **`Level2.unity` is unused** — not the L2 runtime path.
- `LevelSpawnConfig`: pickups, walls, buttonWalls, platforms, springs (`facing`: Up/Right/Left), spikes. Prefer editing the matching `LevelNSpawns` asset over `.unity` YAML. Fans/power buttons spawned from `Level3Layout` (need live refs for wires).

## L1 anchors (SampleScene)
- Floor Y **-3.84** (thickness **0.08**, black). Carl start ~(0, **-3.25**) — ⅓ up screen with camera at y=0.
- Ground spring ~(1, -3.975), size 1.2×0.35 — **top flush with floor top**.
- WinLine Y = `WinLine.DefaultHeight` (**1.31**), full width.
- Spring tops must be walkable from the surface Carl is on (flush or within step-up ~20% of Carl height). Spawn position is the spring **center**, not the top.
- **Spring facing / power:** `SpringPad.Facing` Up/Right/Left — object rotates so local +Y is the launch face; compress + launch along that axis (`CarlLocomotion.Launch`). Per-spring `launchSpeed` in `LevelSpawnConfig` (0 = `DefaultLaunchSpeed` 7.7). Sideways launches use knockback briefly so ground-brake doesn't eat vx on a platform.
- **Spring side-stuck:** Flush upward springs are solid boxes; after Carl stops against one (e.g. blocked by a wall), physics can keep him on a **side** contact (`normal.y ≈ 0`) so the pad never fires and feels like a wall. `SpringPad` also mounts when Carl is grounded with feet at the pad top; `TryStepUp` allows ~0 flush lifts. Keep both if changing spring/step logic.
- Horizontal `DraggableWall` (`vertical: false`) is a sideways moving platform; drag uses `MovePosition` in FixedUpdate. **Carl rides any moving ground** under his feet (`CarlLocomotion` tracks the support collider and applies its position delta each FixedUpdate) — not special-cased per prop.
- One-way platforms: thin lighter deck + corner supports; `PlatformEffector2D`. Solid for LOS (elevated pickups hidden from below). Ignored by start `SnapFeetToGround` so Carl doesn't spawn on a deck above him.
- Spikes: side hit → 25° knockback away (vx preserved; ground-brake disabled during knockback) + 1s grounded decision lock after settle; pointed-face hit → MainMenu. `faceDown` = ceiling spikes (tips down). Not treated as ground; LOS ignores them.
- Fans (`PoweredFan` / `IPowerable`): sprites `Resources/Props/Prop_FanHousing` + `Prop_FanBlades` (true alpha — never ship AI PNGs with baked checkerboard “transparency”). Rules card uses `Prop_FanRules` (housing+blades composite). Powered by `PowerButton`. Facing: Left/Right/Up. On → blades spin + wind streaks; hum while on-camera. Pushes Carl + oil/battery with distance falloff (horizontal adds vx; upward sets vy). **Wind force + streaks are LOS-blocked by solids** (walls, floors, springs, etc.) but **not** by `OneWayPlatform` (wind passes through like Carl rising through a one-way).
- `LinkedWallButton`: one press triggers `ButtonWall.TryTriggerToggle()` on each linked door from its own current position. `ButtonWall` can omit its own button (`hideButton` / `showButton: false`) so only the linked control works.

